# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Ethane: C-C 1.535 A, C-H 1.094 A, H-C-C 111.2 degrees (staggered, D3d).
# Geometry: NIST CCCBDB experimental (Angstrom converted at 1 A = 1.8897261 Bohr); the experimental geometry, not this
# solver's minimum (LSDA on a grid relaxes it slightly: press Relax to see where).
# A 14 Bohr box at h = 0.15 (the app's default grid) under the default ionic potential.
grid 95 0.15
charge 0
ionic accepted
nucleus 6 -1.4504 0.0000 0.0000
nucleus 6 1.4504 0.0000 0.0000
nucleus 1 2.1980 1.9274 0.0000
nucleus 1 2.1980 -0.9637 1.6692
nucleus 1 2.1980 -0.9637 -1.6692
nucleus 1 -2.1980 0.9637 1.6692
nucleus 1 -2.1980 -1.9274 0.0000
nucleus 1 -2.1980 0.9637 -1.6692
